{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"term by term polynomial division term by term polynomial division","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","fileName":"Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Term-by-Term Polynomial Division","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Monomial","Polynomial Long Division","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"term by term polynomial division term by term polynomial division","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","fileName":"Term-by-Term Polynomial Division.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Term-by-Term Polynomial Division","heading":"Term-by-Term Polynomial Division","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Term-by-term polynomial division divides each term of a polynomial numerator by the same [[Monomial]] denominator:\n\n$$\\frac{a+b+c}{d}=\\frac{a}{d}+\\frac{b}{d}+\\frac{c}{d},$$\n\nwhere the quotients are defined. Coefficients divide and exponents on common bases subtract. The method applies to a sum divided by one term, not to a product or to an expression whose divisor has several terms. A multi-term divisor generally requires [[Polynomial Long Division]] or factorization.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Monomial","Polynomial Long Division","algebraessentials.pdf"],"pr